    "request": "a running job twice, a running job while the cluster cannot be reached, a job that never started, a finished job",
    "note": "Real route, no body, no key. A cancel never refuses by state: an ended job answers 200 `already_ended` with `cancelled: false`. The Tapis stand-in carries out the cancel of a running job at once, so the state is already `cancelled`; with the stand-in down the intent is recorded and the job stays live (`cluster_down`)."
